<VI _name="eDyno NVH Accel Simulator.vi" description="eDyno NVH bench self-validation (SW + HW) on a PXIe-4468.\0A\0AAO0 generates a continuous\2C non-regenerated voltage that emulates a PCB 356A15 ICP accelerometer (one axis\2C 100 mV/g) on an e-bike drive unit. AI0 acquires it back through a BNC loopback (AO0 -&gt; AI0) as an acceleration channel with IEPE excitation OFF (never drive an AO into an IEPE-powered input).\0A\0ASpeed: constant\2C or a linear run-up when Run-up Enabled is ON (all orders track speed). Faults can be switched on live from the Fault Injection cluster:\0A1) Imbalance (1x\2C grows with rpm^2) / Misalignment (2x)\0A2) Bearing outer-race defect (BPFO impacts ringing the housing resonance -&gt; crest factor and kurtosis rise\2C sidebands around the resonance)\0A3) Motor torque ripple (6 x pole pairs order) and inverter PWM carrier with +/-2fe sidebands.\0A\0AThe Fault Frequencies indicator shows where each fault should appear in the spectrum at the current speed. Wiring: BNC from AO0 to AI0 on the 4468.\0A\0ALatency: AO is kept about two blocks ahead of AI\2C so a front-panel change shows up in the acquired data after roughly 2 x (Samples per Block / Sample Rate).">

